<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Tilantongo</h1><p class="st-meta">900 CE – 1522 CE (approx.) · capital Tilantongo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The most prestigious Mixtec kingdom of the highlands of Oaxaca, seat of the famous ruler Lord Eight Deer Jaguar Claw.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tilantongo, Ñuu Tnoo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixtecs">Mixtec</a>, emerged as a royal seat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixteca-alta">Mixteca Alta</a> by the 10th century, around 900. Pictorial histories painted on deerskin, such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-bodley">Codex Bodley</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-zouche-nuttall">Codex Zouche-Nuttall</a>, trace its dynasties from that period.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixtecs">Mixtec</a> kingdoms were small city-states ruled by lords and ladies of interlinked noble houses, and Tilantongo was considered the senior line. In the 11th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-deer-jaguar-claw">Lord Eight Deer Jaguar Claw</a>, a lord from Tilantongo, built a wide domain through war and alliance before being sacrificed in 1115. Mixtec artisans were renowned for gold work, turquoise mosaic and painted books.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tilantongo fell under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> tribute in the late 15th century and came under Spanish rule in the 1520s, when its nobles retained some rights as caciques. Its codices are among the most important surviving pre-Hispanic books.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tilantongo.jpg" alt="Tilantongo" width="313" height="463"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tilantongo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 CE – 1522 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tilantongo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lord Eight Deer Jaguar Claw</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mixtec religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mixtec</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ñuu Tnoo, Kingdom of Tilantongo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1211&amp;focus=tilantongo" aria-label="Tilantongo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2036 1537 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tilantongo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2356 1793L2340 1835M2356 1793L2322 1714M2356 1793L2321 1717"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2340 1835h0M2322 1714h0M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2356 1793h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2356 1793h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1211&amp;focus=tilantongo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
